    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are support classes), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line in `AuditOwnerCreated.java` now also logs `membershipNumber` alongside the existing `membershipLevel`, keeping all previously-logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is derived using the same rule as the response DTO (`OwnerMapper`): `customerCode + \"-M\" + last-two-digits-of-registration-year`, returning `null` when either source field is absent. The `coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` test \u2014 which fetches the created owner and asserts the audit line contains both the DTO's `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel` \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` is reported.",
